A||||7||fierogt88||New Member & Suspension Questions||||1||
Z||000000||fierogt88||10-16-2000||04:45 PM||||Hello fellow fiero fans,<P>I'm brand new to the fiero community.  I turned 16 in '88 and wanted the 88 gt real bad, but had to settle for a 78 tbird... yuck.  Anyway, I got one now.  Got my red auto about two months ago in KY.  It needed some work.. suspension mostly, but the interior and body are near mint.  I got a good deal on it because the solenoid in the trans was locking.  BTW, thanx to the fiero owners who helped me push it out of traffic if you happen to lurk here.  My technical question is: what is the deal on the WS6 suspension.  do I have it or is my suspension even better? or is the WS6 any better than the base suspensions?  can anyone clarify the differences for me?<P>TIA<BR>'Gunner'||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||10-16-2000||05:48 PM||||All GT fiero’s and Formula's have the WS6 suspension. The WS6 suspension has stiffer springs, shocks, and control arm bushings also. You also get a rear anti-sway bar that the base coupe does not have. The WS6 suspension rolling stock has 15*7" rear rims with P215/60R15 Goodyear eagle tires and 15*6 front rims with P205/60R15 eagle tires. Basically the WS6 suspension is the performance suspension for the fiero.<P>You also have the best year fiero because in 88 Pontiac redesigned the suspension completely from scratch and mad it a true performance suspension. I hope I don't get flamed for saying this but it is true.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||10-16-2000||05:53 PM||||I forgot to say welcome to the greatest information source for your fiero you will ever find. The people here are great.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||10-16-2000||07:21 PM||||And since you got the best Fiero with the best suspension and the one with the lowest production run you have the least available spare suspension parts out there.  The 88's components are more expensive than the other years.  The car does handle real nice.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierogt88||10-16-2000||09:35 PM||||Ok, that clears up a whole bunch.  So it feels like it handles real good but I can hear a bunch of rattling on the passenger front corner.  I haven't jacked it up but I can grab the top of the tire and rock it back and forth a little and I hear a distinct knocking sound.  I think i saw somewhere that this is probably the lower ball joint.  Am I correct?  How much should one of these go for?||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfiero||10-16-2000||10:12 PM||||It could be the lower ball joint.  With it jacked up in the air have a friend  grab the wheel and move it back and forth while you look at the balljoints (upper & lower), tierod end and upper control arm bushings.<P>If you see any movement at any of these locations something is amiss.<P>Lower ball joints go bad 3-4 times the rate of teh uppers, so if it is a balljoint it'll be the lower.<P>That said....you mentioned that it was coming from the right front corner.....I suspect a bad steering rack bushing.  The part is cheap, but installing it is a pain.<P>Crawl under the car again and grab the shaft that runs from the steering bellow to the tie rod and push up & down on it.  If there is any play at all  here your rack bushing is shot.<P>Good luck and don't let anyone scare you about the availability of '88 parts.  They aren't that tough to come by......and it's worth it for the improved driveablilty.   ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Indiana_resto_guy||10-16-2000||11:39 PM||||Can't check the lower b-joint with out 'unloading' the suspension. Might be the top one though or the wheel brng. Grab the sides of the tire and give it a good rocking, if you hear lots of noise look at the inner tie-rod end. Is your jack tied down well?<BR>Look on the RPO sticker on the front wheel well, left side in the front and look for WS6 on the sticker.<P>Welcome!<p>[This message has been edited by Indiana_resto_guy (edited 10-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Xtreme Fiero's||10-16-2000||11:46 PM||||"WS6" IS NOT THE RPO FOR THE WS6 PACKAGE!!!||||reg||4
